      "writtenOn": "2019-11-14T00:12:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In short, our power budget on 5V is 10A but with everything running full blast we might have demand for up to 12A. We get the remaining 2A back by limiting USB-C to 1.5A and charging ports to 0.9A.\n\nThe assumption is that a port\u0027s power draw is negligible if it\u0027s not overcurrent, so the available power budget can be computed from overcurrent inputs and the two available knobs (USB-C and charging port power) twiddled as required stay under budget.",
      "parentUuid": "87e3dad3_3d400317",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "77fe4f92ffa7a48cd9b4fdc5e68bd4b35a0d7f1a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
